 except Moses (forgetting the iniurie he had receiued, 

which was no lesse then a pretence to stone him to death) had succoured and relieued their distressed  
                         fortunes.

following_english_context:
The Hebrewes hauing thus put their enemies to flight, foraged the whole Region, and caried and droue away with them a great pray; and killing all the inhabitants threof both men & women, they only spared the virgins (for this commaund had Phinees receiued from Moses hand
                           •…
                        ) who returning home with his armie in safetie, brought with him a memorable and mightie pray of Oxen, fiftie  and two thousand, sixtie and seuen: of Asses, sixtie thousand: of golden and siluer vessels a great number (which those of that countrey were wont to vse in their domesticall affaires.) For by  reason of their great riches, they liued verie delicately: there were

